# Answer key for the "pharma-supply" gold dataset (Postgres) — HUMAN-MAINTAINED.
# Wave B1.b of Milestone 1.23 (F1.23.4): statistical-power wave.
# Story: generics manufacturer integrating two contract-manufacturing sites — serialisation
# FKs re-added NOT VALID, WMS receipts landing without constraints, legacy LIMS still read.
# See ./README.md for the planted-defect table.
#
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"sites","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: contact_email is null for 12% (41/340) of sites — the acquired sites were loaded from a spreadsheet that had a phone column but no mailbox, so recall notifications have no addressee."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"sites","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 22 contact_email values hold a distribution-list description rather than an address (\"QA team - see intranet\") — they fail the email format."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"sites","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 14 mobile_number values are internal extension codes (\"x4471\") — they fail the phone format, so the out-of-hours escalation chain breaks at those sites."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"sites","field":"gln_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 6 duplicate GLN codes on the declared UNIQUE key — the acquired sites reused the parent group's location numbers for their own warehouses."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"supply","entity":"products","field":"dosage_form_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: dosage_form_cd stored as TAB / tab / Tab / CAPS / caps ... — 64 raw values collapse to 51 normalized, so dosage-form volumes are split across spellings."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"products","field":"info_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: info_url is null for 16% (1984/12400) of products — the SmPC link was only backfilled for products still marketed in the EU, so the rest have no leaflet reference."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"products","field":"info_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 340 info_url values are file-server paths (\"\\\\qa-share\\smpc\\…\") rather than URLs — they fail the url format."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"supply","entity":"products","field":"discontinued_on","severity":"medium","note":"planted: discontinued_on carries a 2099-12-31 sentinel for \"still marketed\" — a future date in the column that portfolio planning reads to decide what to keep making."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"products","field":"gtin","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 40 duplicate GTINs on the declared UNIQUE key — pack variants acquired with the second site carry the barcode of the parent group's equivalent pack."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"batches","field":"batch_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2400 batch_uuid values are the site's own 10-character batch token rather than a UUID — they fail the uuid format and break the serialisation handshake with the EU hub."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"batches","field":"release_status_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: release_status_cd is null on 9% (84600/940000) of batches — batches made under tolling agreements are released in the partner's system, so this column cannot answer \"what is releasable\"."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"batches","field":"batch_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 1240 duplicate batch numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — the acquired sites number batches per line rather than per company, so the same number recurs across sites."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipments","field":"carrier_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: carrier_cd is null on 8% (328000/4100000) of shipments — customer-collect orders carry no carrier, and so do the shipments the acquired sites booked by phone, which is why lane cost analysis is incomplete."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipment_lines","field":"customer_ref","severity":"medium","note":"planted: customer_ref is null on 17% (3128000/18400000) of lines — EDI orders carry the reference, portal orders do not, so half the dispute investigations start with nothing to search on."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"cold_chain_readings","field":"excursion_flag_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: excursion_flag_cd is null on 8% (6880000/86000000) of readings — the evaluation step times out on long journeys, so those readings are neither \"in range\" nor \"excursion\"."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"supply","entity":"cold_chain_readings","field":"recorded_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest recorded_at is 2024-06-30 (773 days stale) — the IoT logger contract lapsed and the gateway stopped writing, but the excursion dashboard still reads this table and shows a clean cold chain."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"v_batch_status","field":"batch_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view is specified as one row per batch, but the join to the multi-row deviation list fans out and leaves 3600 duplicate batch_id values — \"batches on hold\" is over-counted."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"supply","entity":"v_batch_status","field":"yield_pct","severity":"medium","note":"planted: yield_pct maxes at 112.6 in a column named as a percentage — actual output is divided by a theoretical yield that excludes reprocessed material, so batches appear to produce more than their input allows."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"supply","entity":"v_batch_status","field":"released_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: released_at is null for 10% (94000/940000) of batches — batches never released and batches released in a partner system are indistinguishable in the view."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_wms_receipts","field":"receipt_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 93600 duplicate receipt_id values in the WMS landing table — the warehouse system re-sends the day's receipts after every failed acknowledgement, and nothing de-duplicates before the merge."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_wms_receipts","field":"receipt_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 48000 receipt_date values arrive as DD.MM.YYYY from the German site's WMS instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_wms_receipts","field":"qty_received","severity":"low","note":"planted: qty_received uses -9999 as the WMS \"quantity unknown\" sentinel — a negative in a receipt-quantity column that inventory reconciliation adds up as if it were real."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_wms_receipts","field":"posting_ts","severity":"medium","note":"planted: posting_ts reaches 2087-03-01 — a handheld terminal with a wrong system clock posts receipts sixty years ahead, and the load accepts them."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_product_master","field":"product_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 114 duplicate product_id values in the master landing table — the two acquired sites' catalogues overlap on the products transferred between them."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_product_master","field":"launch_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 620 launch_date values are the string \"PENDING\" written for products awaiting marketing authorisation — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"quality","entity":"deviations","field":"batch_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: batch_id is null on 15% (12600/84000) of deviations — facility and utility deviations legitimately have no batch, but so do 2000 product deviations raised before the batch was known, and the column cannot separate them."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"quality","entity":"deviations","field":"severity_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: severity_cd stored as CRITICAL / critical / Critical / MAJOR / major ... — 14 raw values collapse to 9 normalized, so the regulator-facing severity split is wrong."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"quality","entity":"deviations","field":"raised_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: raised_on reaches back to 1899-01-05 — the legacy QMS wrote its epoch date wherever the raise date was blank on import, so \"oldest open deviation\" is nonsense."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"quality","entity":"deviations","field":"deviation_ref","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 210 duplicate deviation_ref values on the declared UNIQUE key — the acquired sites' reference series restarted each year, so the same reference exists for several years."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"quality","entity":"capa_actions","field":"owner_dept","severity":"medium","note":"planted: owner_dept is null on 12% (5040/42000) of CAPAs — actions migrated from the acquired sites lost their owning department, so overdue-CAPA escalation has nobody to escalate to."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"quality","entity":"capa_actions","field":"days_open","severity":"low","note":"planted: days_open reaches -3 — CAPAs closed with a backdated closure date produce negative durations, which pull the average closure time down."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"quality","entity":"lab_tests","field":"result_value","severity":"low","note":"planted: result_value reaches -12.4 — assay results are stored in the same column as blank-corrected absorbances, and a mis-mapped method writes negatives into a column that cannot be negative for a potency test."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"quality","entity":"lab_tests","field":"analyst_initials","severity":"low","note":"planted: analyst_initials is null on 8% (192000/2400000) of tests — instrument-integrated results are written by the system with no analyst, which breaks the data-integrity requirement to attribute every result to a person."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"quality","entity":"stability_studies","field":"deviation_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: deviation_id is null on 90% (16560/18400) of studies — routine stability studies have no triggering deviation, but the column is also the only link for the 240 studies opened BECAUSE of one, and those links were lost on migration."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"quality","entity":"stability_studies","field":"started_on, ended_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: the whole ended_on range (2010-01-01 … 2025-12-01) precedes the whole started_on range (2011-03-01 … 2026-07-01) — the two columns were transposed when the acquired site's stability register was mapped."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"quality","entity":"v_batch_release","field":"batch_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the release view is specified as one row per batch, but batches with more than one release decision (release, then partial recall) appear twice — 8400 duplicate batch_id values."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"quality","entity":"v_batch_release","field":"qp_name","severity":"low","note":"planted: qp_name is null for 5% (47000/940000) of rows — the Qualified Person who released the batch was not carried across for tolling partners, which is exactly the attribution a regulator asks for first."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"quality","entity":"stg_lab_import","field":"test_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 14400 duplicate test_id values in the instrument-import landing table — chromatography systems re-export a sequence whenever it is re-processed, and both copies land."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"quality","entity":"stg_lab_import","field":"tested_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 26000 tested_date values arrive as MM/DD/YY from the US site's instruments instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format, and the ambiguous ones silently parse to the wrong day."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"quality","entity":"legacy_lims_results","field":"result_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 21600 duplicate result_id values — the legacy LIMS re-issued the full result set on every amendment, so trending double-counts amended results."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"quality","entity":"legacy_lims_results","field":"tested_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: tested_on reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written by the original loader wherever the test date was blank."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"quality","entity":"legacy_lims_results","field":"reported_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest reported_at is 2023-09-29 (1048 days stale) — the pre-acquisition LIMS was frozen at go-live, but three trend reports still read it and present its results as current."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"batches","field":"product_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 6400 batches reference a product_id with no products row — discontinued SKUs were deleted from the catalogue while their batches stayed for retention."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipments","field":"site_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 12000 shipments dispatch from a site that no longer exists — the third-party warehouses dropped after the network review were purged from the site master."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipment_lines","field":"shipment_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 84000 shipment lines have no parent shipment — cancelled shipments are deleted by the order sync and leave their lines behind."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipment_lines","field":"batch_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 31000 shipment lines reference a batch that was purged — the traceability chain from customer back to manufacture is broken for those lines."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"cold_chain_readings","field":"shipment_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 1240000 logger readings reference deleted shipments — the temperature history cannot be attached to any delivery."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"quality","entity":"deviations","field":"batch_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 3400 deviations reference a batch that no longer exists — the cross-schema FK was left NOT VALID after the batch purge, so the quality record points at nothing."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"quality","entity":"lab_tests","field":"batch_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 18400 lab results reference a purged batch — results that can never be tied back to product."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"quality","entity":"capa_actions","field":"deviation_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 940 CAPA actions reference a deviation that was deleted rather than voided, so the corrective action has no cause on file."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"batches","field":"site_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2100 batches name a manufacturing site that is not in the site master — no FK was declared on this column, so tolling-partner site codes were loaded verbatim."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"shipments","field":"product_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 8600 shipments carry a product_id with no catalogue row — the header-level product code is written by the order feed without validation."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"v_batch_status","field":"batch_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view carries 3600 batch_id values with no batch row — it reads the WMS landing table, which still holds batches deleted from the core."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"supply","entity":"stg_product_master","field":"product_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 114 rows in the master landing table reference products deleted between extract and load."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"quality","entity":"stability_studies","field":"deviation_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 180 stability studies reference a deviation id that does not exist — the acquired site's reference numbers were copied into the column without re-keying."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"supply","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on supply.supply_contracts_vault (commercially sensitive tolling agreements) — 1 of 10 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"quality","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on quality.quality_audit_vault (regulator correspondence held under legal privilege) — 1 of 8 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
